return [
    '/printers-consumables/' => 'Printers and consumables cover everything your office needs to put ink and toner onto paper, from single-function desktop machines to shared workgroup devices, copiers, scanners, plotters and the cartridges that keep them running. This is where most Nigerian businesses, schools and government offices spend repeatedly, so the smart decision is rarely about the machine alone. It is about the total cost of ownership across its working life: the purchase, the running cost per page, the yield of each cartridge and how easily you can source genuine supplies afterwards. Browse the subcategories to compare printers by technology, copiers for high-volume departments, scanners for digitising records, and the full range of ink and toner. As you choose, weigh your real monthly print volume against a device\'s rated duty cycle, decide between inkjet and laser for your workload, and plan for Nigeria\'s power realities by pairing any machine with a surge protector or inverter-friendly UPS. OfficeLand stocks HP, Canon, Epson and Brother hardware alongside genuine cartridges, with nationwide delivery from our Victoria Island showrooms on Idowu Martins Street, Lagos. Tell us your volumes and the environment the device will work in, and request a quote; our team replies within four working hours.',

    '/printers-consumables/copiers/' => 'Copiers and multifunction copiers are built for the shared, high-volume workload that would quickly wear out a desktop printer: the central machine a whole department, school office or government registry feeds all day. Modern copiers do far more than photocopy. Most combine printing, scanning and copying, handle double-sided output automatically, collate and staple finished sets, and connect over the network so many staff can send jobs from their own desks. When choosing one, start with your monthly page count and match it honestly to the copier\'s rated duty cycle, because buying under your real volume is the fastest route to breakdowns and downtime. Look closely at the cost per page and the yield of its toner and drum units, since consumables, not the machine, dominate long-term spend. Favour genuine toner to protect your warranty and keep output sharp, and be wary of counterfeit cartridges, which are common in the Nigerian market and can damage expensive imaging units. Given the state of mains power in Lagos and beyond, install any copier on a stabiliser or UPS to guard against surges. OfficeLand supplies business copiers and genuine consumables with delivery across Nigeria from our Victoria Island base. Share your volumes and workflow needs and request a quote within four working hours.',

    '/printers-consumables/ink-toner/' => 'Ink and toner is the consumables heart of any print operation, the recurring purchase that quietly decides whether your printing is affordable over a year. This section brings together everything that feeds your machines: ink cartridges for inkjet printers, toner cartridges for laser printers and copiers, and the drums and maintenance kits that keep both running cleanly. The single most important rule is to buy the exact cartridge your printer model takes, so always check the device\'s model number before ordering. Beyond fit, the numbers that matter are page yield and cost per page, which together tell you the true running cost rather than the headline price of a single cartridge. Genuine consumables protect your printer warranty, deliver consistent colour and density, and spare you the clogged heads, streaking and leaks that cheap imitations cause. This matters acutely in Nigeria, where counterfeit cartridges circulate widely and a bad refill can cost more than it saves. OfficeLand supplies genuine HP, Canon, Epson and Brother ink and toner, matched to your machines and delivered nationwide from Victoria Island, Lagos. Browse the subcategories below, or tell us your printer models and request a quote answered within four working hours.',

    '/printers-consumables/ink-toner/drums-maintenance-kits/' => 'Drums and maintenance kits are the service parts that keep laser printers and copiers producing clean pages long after the first toner runs out. The drum, or imaging unit, is the component that actually transfers toner onto paper; as it wears it begins to show as faint lines, grey backgrounds, repeating marks or patchy coverage, which are the usual signs it needs replacing. Maintenance kits bundle the wear items a busy machine consumes over time, such as fusers, transfer rollers and feed rollers, and are designed to be fitted at set page intervals to prevent jams and keep print quality stable. When ordering, match the drum or kit precisely to your printer or copier model, because these parts are not interchangeable across ranges. On some machines the drum is built into the toner cartridge, while on others it is a separate long-life unit, so confirm which design yours uses before buying. Genuine drums and kits are worth insisting on: they are engineered to the machine\'s tolerances, protect your warranty and avoid the premature failures that counterfeit parts bring. OfficeLand stocks genuine drums and maintenance kits for Brother, HP, Canon and Epson devices, delivered anywhere in Nigeria. Send us your model number and request a quote within four working hours.',

    '/printers-consumables/ink-toner/ink-cartridges/' => 'Ink cartridges are the consumables that feed inkjet printers, and choosing the right ones keeps your colour documents, photos and everyday prints looking sharp while controlling cost. Inkjet machines use either separate cartridges for each colour, which let you replace only the colour that runs out, or a combined tri-colour cartridge alongside black. Some also take pigment-based black for crisp text and dye-based colour for vivid images, so check what your model requires before you order. The figures that decide value are page yield and cost per page, and high-yield or XL cartridges usually work out cheaper for offices that print often. Always buy genuine cartridges: they keep the warranty valid, resist the drying and clogging that plague printheads in Nigeria\'s warm, dusty conditions, and avoid the leaks and faded output common with counterfeit ink. Store spare cartridges sealed and away from heat, and if a machine sits idle for long stretches run an occasional print to keep the nozzles clear. OfficeLand supplies genuine HP, Canon, Epson and Brother ink cartridges, including popular HP ink cartridges in Nigeria, matched to your printer and delivered nationwide from Victoria Island, Lagos. Tell us your printer model and request a quote answered within four working hours.',

    '/printers-consumables/ink-toner/toner-cartridges/' => 'Toner cartridges supply the fine powder that laser printers and copiers fuse onto the page, and they are the backbone of fast, low-cost mono and colour printing in busy offices. Compared with ink, toner delivers a much higher page yield and a lower cost per page, which is why organisations with heavy document volumes favour laser. Colour laser devices use four cartridges, cyan, magenta, yellow and black, while mono machines use black alone; high-yield versions cut your cost per page further if you print in volume. Match the cartridge exactly to your printer or copier model, and note whether your machine uses an all-in-one cartridge with the drum built in or a separate drum unit, as this changes what you reorder. Genuine toner matters: it protects your warranty, gives consistent density and clean text, and avoids the leaks, poor adhesion and imaging-unit damage that counterfeit toner causes, a real risk in the Nigerian market. OfficeLand stocks genuine HP toner cartridges in Nigeria alongside Canon and Brother toner, all matched to your devices and delivered nationwide from our Lagos showrooms. Send your model numbers and request a quote; we reply within four working hours.',

    '/printers-consumables/printers/' => 'Printers are the workhorses of any office, and this section gathers the full range so you can match the right machine to the right job. Whether you need a compact inkjet for a single desk, a fast laser for a busy department, an all-in-one that prints, scans and copies, or a large-format plotter for drawings and banners, the choice turns on the same few questions. How many pages will you print each month, and does that sit comfortably within the machine\'s duty cycle? Do you print mostly black text, where laser excels, or colour and photos, where inkjet often wins? What is the running cost once you factor in cartridge yields and cost per page, rather than just the price on the box? Connectivity matters too: USB for a single user, Ethernet or Wi-Fi for shared network printing, and mobile printing for staff working from phones and tablets. In Nigeria, plan for power stability by placing any printer on a surge protector or UPS to avoid damage during outages and spikes. OfficeLand carries HP, Canon, Epson and Brother printers with genuine consumables and nationwide delivery from Victoria Island, Lagos. Explore the subcategories, then tell us your workload and request a quote within four working hours.',

    '/printers-consumables/printers/all-in-one-printers/' => 'All-in-one printers, also called multifunction printers, combine printing, scanning, copying and often faxing in a single device, which makes them the practical choice for offices, small businesses, schools and home workers who want one machine to do everything. They come in both inkjet and laser forms: inkjet all-in-ones suit mixed colour work and occasional photo printing, while laser all-in-ones handle high text volumes faster and at a lower cost per page. When choosing, look beyond the print engine to the features that save time daily, such as an automatic document feeder for scanning and copying multi-page documents, automatic double-sided printing, and network or Wi-Fi connectivity so several staff can share the device. Match the machine\'s duty cycle to your real monthly volume, and compare cartridge yields and running costs before deciding. Insist on genuine ink or toner to keep the warranty intact and output reliable, and avoid the counterfeit consumables common in the local market. As with any office electronics in Nigeria, protect the unit with a surge protector or UPS against unstable power. OfficeLand stocks HP, Canon, Epson and Brother all-in-one printers with genuine cartridges, delivered nationwide from Victoria Island, Lagos. Tell us how you will use it and request a quote within four working hours.',

    '/printers-consumables/printers/inkjet-printers/' => 'Inkjet printers spray liquid ink onto paper and remain the go-to choice when you need good colour, photo-quality images or low-cost entry into printing. They handle a wide range of paper types and sizes, reproduce colour gradients smoothly, and generally cost less to buy than laser machines, which makes them popular for home offices, small businesses and anywhere colour matters more than sheer speed. The trade-off is running cost: ink cartridges yield fewer pages than toner, so for very high volumes a laser printer may prove cheaper over time. Look for models with separate colour cartridges so you replace only the colour that runs out, and consider high-yield cartridges if you print regularly. Some ranges use refillable ink-tank systems that lower cost per page considerably for busy users. In Nigeria\'s climate, inkjet heads can dry if a machine sits unused, so print occasionally to keep nozzles clear, and always fit genuine ink to protect the warranty and avoid clogging from counterfeit refills. Pair the printer with a surge protector against unstable mains power. OfficeLand supplies Canon, Epson, HP and Brother inkjet printers in Lagos with genuine ink and nationwide delivery. Share your needs and request a quote answered within four working hours.',

    '/printers-consumables/printers/large-format-plotters/' => 'Large format printers and plotters handle output that ordinary office machines cannot: architectural and engineering drawings, construction and survey plans, maps, technical schematics, posters, banners and signage. They print onto wide media, commonly A1, A0 and roll paper, and are built for the precise lines and accurate scaling that design, construction, surveying and print-for-hire businesses depend on. When choosing, start with the widest media you need to produce and confirm the machine supports it, then consider whether your work is line-based CAD output or colour-rich graphics and photographic posters, as these favour different ink configurations. Check the ink system and the yield of its cartridges or tanks, since wide-format consumables are a significant ongoing cost, and look at connectivity and the ability to accept the file formats your drawing or design software produces. Genuine inks matter here more than anywhere, because colour accuracy and line sharpness are the whole point, and counterfeit ink undermines both while voiding the warranty. In Nigeria, protect these substantial investments with proper surge protection and stable power. OfficeLand supplies large format printers and plotters from brands including Canon, Epson and HP, with genuine consumables and nationwide delivery from Lagos. Tell us your media sizes and workload, and request a quote within four working hours.',

    '/printers-consumables/printers/laser-printers/' => 'Laser printers use toner and a heated fusing process to produce crisp text and fast output at a low cost per page, which makes them the standard choice for offices, schools and government departments that print in volume. Compared with inkjet, laser machines print faster, deliver sharper black text and give a far higher page yield per cartridge, so the cost per page falls as your volume rises. They come as mono models, ideal for document-heavy workloads, and colour models for reports, presentations and marketing material. When choosing, match the printer\'s rated duty cycle to your real monthly page count, compare toner yields and cost per page across models, and decide whether you need network or Wi-Fi printing for a shared office or just USB for one desk. Insist on genuine toner to keep the warranty valid and avoid the leaks and imaging damage caused by the counterfeit cartridges common in the Nigerian market. Because laser printers draw a heavy current when the fuser heats, place them on a surge protector or an adequately rated UPS to survive unstable mains power. OfficeLand stocks HP, Canon and Brother laser printers in Lagos with genuine toner and nationwide delivery. Tell us your volumes and request a quote within four working hours.',

    '/printers-consumables/scanners/' => 'Scanners turn paper into digital files, and they are essential wherever an organisation needs to archive records, share documents electronically or cut down on physical storage. This matters for Nigerian offices, schools and government bodies digitising registries, invoices, contracts and forms. Dedicated scanners come in several forms: flatbed scanners for books, bound documents and delicate originals; sheet-fed and document scanners with an automatic document feeder for processing stacks of pages quickly; and compact portable units for fieldwork. When choosing, consider the optical resolution you need, higher for photographs and detailed images, standard for everyday text documents, and the daily volume the scanner is rated to handle. Duplex scanning captures both sides of a page in one pass and saves considerable time on double-sided paperwork, while reliable software that produces searchable PDFs makes archives far easier to use. Check connectivity and whether the scanner integrates with your network and document systems. If you also need to print and copy, an all-in-one printer may serve better than a standalone scanner. OfficeLand supplies scanners from Canon, Epson, HP and Brother, with nationwide delivery from our Victoria Island showrooms in Lagos. Tell us your document volumes and workflow, and request a quote answered within four working hours.',
];
